@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2038 = private unnamed_addr constant [757 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `assert` statements in `except` clauses.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWhen testing for exceptions, `pytest.raises()` should be used instead of\0A`assert` statements in `except` clauses, as it's more explicit and\0Aidiomatic. Further, `pytest.raises()` will fail if the exception is _not_\0Araised, unlike the `assert` statement.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef test_foo():\0A    try:\0A        1 / 0\0A    except ZeroDivisionError as e:\0A        assert e.args\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0Adef test_foo():\0A    with pytest.raises(ZeroDivisionError) as exc_info:\0A        1 / 0\0A    assert exc_info.value.args\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [`pytest` documentation: `pytest.raises`](https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/reference.html#pytest-raises)\0A", align 1
