@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2044 = private unnamed_addr constant [561 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `assert` statements whose test expression is a falsy value.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`pytest.fail` conveys the intent more clearly than `assert falsy_value`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef test_foo():\0A    if some_condition:\0A        assert False, \22some_condition was True\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0Adef test_foo():\0A    if some_condition:\0A        pytest.fail(\22some_condition was True\22)\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [`pytest` documentation: `pytest.fail`](https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/reference.html#pytest-fail)\0A", align 1
