@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2047 = private unnamed_addr constant [647 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of assertion methods from the `unittest` module.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ATo make use of `pytest`'s assertion rewriting, a regular `assert` statement\0Ais preferred over `unittest`'s assertion methods.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport unittest\0A\0A\0Aclass TestFoo(unittest.TestCase):\0A    def test_foo(self):\0A        self.assertEqual(a, b)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport unittest\0A\0A\0Aclass TestFoo(unittest.TestCase):\0A    def test_foo(self):\0A        assert a == b\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [`pytest` documentation: Assertion introspection details](https://docs.pytest.org/en/7.1.x/how-to/assert.html#assertion-introspection-details)\0A", align 1
