@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2106 = private unnamed_addr constant [2184 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the type of parameter values passed to `pytest.mark.parametrize`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `argvalues` argument of `pytest.mark.parametrize` takes an iterator of\0Aparameter values, which can be provided as lists or tuples.\0A\0ATo aid in readability, it's recommended to use a consistent style for the\0Alist of values rows, and, in the case of multiple parameters, for each row\0Aof values.\0A\0AThe style for the list of values rows can be configured via the\0A[`lint.flake8-pytest-style.parametrize-values-type`] setting, while the\0Astyle for each row of values can be configured via the\0A[`lint.flake8-pytest-style.parametrize-values-row-type`] setting.\0A\0AFor example, [`lint.flake8-pytest-style.parametrize-values-type`] will lead to\0Athe following expectations:\0A\0A- `tuple`: `@pytest.mark.parametrize(\22value\22, (\22a\22, \22b\22, \22c\22))`\0A- `list`: `@pytest.mark.parametrize(\22value\22, [\22a\22, \22b\22, \22c\22])`\0A\0ASimilarly, [`lint.flake8-pytest-style.parametrize-values-row-type`] will lead to\0Athe following expectations:\0A\0A- `tuple`: `@pytest.mark.parametrize((\22key\22, \22value\22), [(\22a\22, \22b\22), (\22c\22, \22d\22)])`\0A- `list`: `@pytest.mark.parametrize((\22key\22, \22value\22), [[\22a\22, \22b\22], [\22c\22, \22d\22]])`\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0A# expected list, got tuple\0A@pytest.mark.parametrize(\22param\22, (1, 2))\0Adef test_foo(param): ...\0A\0A\0A# expected top-level list, got tuple\0A@pytest.mark.parametrize(\0A    (\22param1\22, \22param2\22),\0A    (\0A        (1, 2),\0A        (3, 4),\0A    ),\0A)\0Adef test_bar(param1, param2): ...\0A\0A\0A# expected individual rows to be tuples, got lists\0A@pytest.mark.parametrize(\0A    (\22param1\22, \22param2\22),\0A    [\0A        [1, 2],\0A        [3, 4],\0A    ],\0A)\0Adef test_baz(param1, param2): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0A@pytest.mark.parametrize(\22param\22, [1, 2, 3])\0Adef test_foo(param): ...\0A\0A\0A@pytest.mark.parametrize((\22param1\22, \22param2\22), [(1, 2), (3, 4)])\0Adef test_bar(param1, param2): ...\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-pytest-style.parametrize-values-type`\0A- `lint.flake8-pytest-style.parametrize-values-row-type`\0A\0A## References\0A- [`pytest` documentation: How to parametrize fixtures and test functions](https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/how-to/parametrize.html#pytest-mark-parametrize)\0A", align 1
