@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2141 = private unnamed_addr constant [575 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `else` statements with a `raise` statement in the preceding `if`\0Ablock.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `else` statement is not needed as the `raise` statement will always\0Abreak out of the current scope. Removing the `else` will reduce nesting\0Aand make the code more readable.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef foo(bar, baz):\0A    if bar == \22Specific Error\22:\0A        raise Exception(bar)\0A    else:\0A        raise Exception(baz)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef foo(bar, baz):\0A    if bar == \22Specific Error\22:\0A        raise Exception(bar)\0A    raise Exception(baz)\0A```\0A", align 1
